      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could the message say what goes wrong without this patch, e.g. that an aliased slice makes smaps report the whole 16KB page as shared? \"instead of native folio mapcount\" doesn\u0027t quite match what aosp/4312510 does today: `vma_slice_ptes()` already discounts this mm\u0027s own slice PTEs, so the difference is the per-slice split for pages that are also mapped elsewhere.\n\nIt would also help to mention the anonymous and THP changes and the new rmap walk on every read, and to say \"4KB processes\" rather than \"compat slices\".",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "b25d36dc2ebafabbe4adb3b838cbc0270732624c",
