    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "75c3ce9c_2ce1922c",
        "filename": "fs/proc/task_mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 1147,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T21:42:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried this reports anonymous pages that a 4KB process shares with its child after `fork()` as private. `DIV_ROUND_UP(folio_mapcount(folio), P3S_SLICES_PER_PAGE)` is 1 whenever the mapcount is 4 or less, so a page with one or two slices mapped in both parent and child is Private in both, where `vma_slice_ptes()` (aosp/4312510) reports it as shared. A whole private page (four slice PTEs) is already Private with full PSS today.\n\nThe same goes for pagemap: with `vma_slice_ptes()` gone from `pte_to_pagemap_entry()`, anonymous pages now need `folio_precise_page_mapcount() \u003d\u003d 1`, so a private anonymous page mapped by its four slice PTEs loses PM_MMAP_EXCLUSIVE.\n\nUnlike swap entries (aosp/4393889), present PTEs can be counted exactly, and the commit message only mentions file slices. Would it be OK to drop this hunk and keep `vma_slice_ptes()` for anonymous pages in both places?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "b25d36dc2ebafabbe4adb3b838cbc0270732624c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3698d940_c7a85ab8",
        "filename": "fs/proc/task_mmu.c",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 1200,
      "author": {
        "id": 1499410
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T21:42:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the per-slice counts stay, would you mind moving the rmap part out of task_mmu.c? Together with the pagemap loop, this adds about 200 lines of P3S-only code to a core file.\n\n`ppps_file_mapcount_one()` and `ppps_file_page_mapcounts()` don\u0027t depend on procfs internals and could go next to `vma_slice_ptes()` in `include/linux/p3s/proc.h` (or into `mm/p3s.c`), so that task_mmu.c keeps only the PTE loops and the dispatch.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "b25d36dc2ebafabbe4adb3b838cbc0270732624c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
